Subject: Tweak: match point
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

A match to a number of goals has nothing like overtime's sudden death: when
time runs out with the scores level, cGame::InitGameState queues the
"SuddenDeath" event, whose listeners play overtime's music
(cGame::OnSuddenDeath, PlaySuddenDeathMusic) and its siren and lights at the
four corners of the field (Presentation::OnSuddenDeath,
PlayGoalEffects("Goal_suddendeath")), and the HUD shows SUDDEN DEATH where
the clock is (HUDClock::Update).

With "Match point" enabled, in a match to a number of goals (not in Strikers
101 or the Striker Challenges), the kickoff that finds both teams one goal
from winning queues that same event: siren, lights and music. The music
replaces the stadium's, as in overtime (GS_OVERTIME stops it): that kickoff
stops the stadium's music, and GS_GAMEPLAY no longer starts or resumes it
while both teams are one goal from winning. The sudden death music plays on
until the match ends, stopped at GS_END_GAME as after overtime. The HUD
shows SUDDEN DEATH instead of "First to" in the same case. A team alone one
goal from winning changes nothing. In a match to one goal, both are from the
first kickoff.

None of it touches the match: the music is the audio's, which no rollback
restores and a replayed frame does not start again, the lights draw from
the effects' own random seed (gEffectsRandomSeed), and the HUD reads the
scores. Two games playing each other may differ in it.

